ll chrony recovery/re-sync after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed chrony on node1 and node2 (Ubuntu 24.04 ships only systemd-timesyncd, which is client-only)\",\"systemd-timesyncd was removed/superseded automatically by the chrony install on both nodes\",\"Confirmed node1 has no real external internet/NTP reachability, so configured it as a standalone authoritative source instead of depending on public pools\",\"On node1: removed default pool ntp.ubuntu.com lines from /etc/chrony/chrony.conf, added 'local stratum 10' and 'allow 10.100.87.0/24', restarted chrony\",\"On node2: removed default pool lines, added 'server 10.100.87.10 iburst', restarted chrony\",\"Verified node2 selected node1 as its synced source (chronyc sources shows ^* against Reference ID 0A64570A = 10.100.87.10) and node1 shows node2 as a connected NTP client via chronyc clients\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and chrony health baseline on both nodes\",\"Restarted node1 via sudo reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified chrony active and local-stratum config intact\",\"Confirmed node2 (which stayed up throughout node1's restart) continued tracking node1 without config loss\",\"Restarted node2 via sudo reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified chrony active, config intact, and re-synced to node1 as source (^* Reference ID 0A64570A, stratum 11)\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 configured as internal time source (own reference clock, serving node2)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-308bc7a1ec0044e3\",\"cmd-4b22c668c1ee4177\",\"cmd-69a3979a8ec041a2\"],\"summary\":\"chrony.conf on node1 set to local stratum 10 with allow 10.100.87.0/24; chronyc tracking shows Reference ID 7F7F0101 (self) stratum 10; chronyc clients shows node2 (vm-rhel8-4189848754) polling it\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 configured to sync against node1 instead of a public time server\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4634cd216b9f4891\",\"cmd-26b47b248a554ce8\",\"cmd-69dea7d4a3a943ff\"],\"summary\":\"chrony.conf on node2 has only 'server 10.100.87.10 iburst', no pool lines; chronyc sources shows ^* selected source with Reference ID 0A64570A = 10.100.87.10 (node1), stratum 11\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 pre-restart healthy baseline (boot identity, chrony health)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-79421456d6ca4497\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id dfeb3b70-bc1e-4ce9-90d0-9c9c853416e7 and chrony active/tracking stratum 10 before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a4f32d52528b464c\",\"cmd-158c1f482b6d4c01\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sudo reboot' returned acknowledgement before disconnect; subsequent poll timed out confirming node1 was down\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 changed boot identity after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-dbe72062c6ef4cbc\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id changed to 19f1bc96-6b73-430b-8cc0-1f3f3ec842ad, proving an actual reboot occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery of required service/config\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-080633b5ec054087\"],\"summary\":\"chrony active again, chronyc tracking shows Reference ID 7F7F0101 stratum 10, and chrony.conf still contains 'local stratum 10' / 'allow 10.100.87.0/24'\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 pre-restart healthy baseline (boot identity, chrony health, synced to node1)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a211f2f9640e47ed\",\"cmd-23fea19636ff4769\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id bdd5de93-e94e-4d33-8384-6a01c51a3d49; chronyc sources/tracking confirmed still synced to node1 after node1's own restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement and disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-16fac97be5f34063\",\"cmd-9bb16f0f6cbd4e07\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sudo reboot' returned acknowledgement before disconnect; subsequent poll timed out confirming node2 was down\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 changed boot identity after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fc7bd93dd3014f85\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id changed to 79870bec-3386-488d